# Pd's inlet~ and outlet~ allocate a reblocker at creation (g_io.c:320, 688) that their free functions
# do not free: 54 bytes per signal inlet or outlet of an abstraction, per load. Upstream.
leak:vinlet_newsig
leak:voutlet_newsig
# canvas_setargs keeps the last abstraction's arguments in a static until the next call. Bounded.
leak:canvas_setargs
# Pd's [table] gives its canvas a gstub (g_canvas.c:453) that is not freed: 16 bytes per [table], per load.
leak:table_donew
# Pd's [expr] keeps each function or table name it parses (x_vexp.c:2186): a few bytes per name, per load. Upstream.
leak:getoken
# Pd's [clone] connects each instance's outlets (g_clone.c:221) and does not free the connections: 16 bytes per
# instance outlet, per load. Upstream.
leak:clone_initinstance
# A gstub that glist_init gives a canvas (g_canvas.c:453) outlives some canvases, such as [text define]'s: 16
# bytes each, per load. Upstream.
leak:glist_init
# Pd's [text search] (x_text.c:1267) and [netreceive] (x_net.c:629) keep a few bytes past their free. Upstream.
leak:text_search_new
leak:netreceive_closeall
# An abstraction's [declare -path /absolute] (g_canvas.c canvas_path) is not freed with the canvas: 16 bytes per
# path, per load. Upstream.
leak:canvas_declare
